{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>It staggers.</b> The meaning concerns the inhabitants of the earth, that they will flee from place to place and wander about like a watchman, for the watchman changes the place of his lodging:" "And the meaning of <b>and is heavy.</b> is that they will seek to move and to flee, but their transgression weighs heavy upon them, and they fall:" "<b>Rises.</b> Noun of action, and likewise וּמֶלֶךְ אַלְקוּם עִמּוֹ (Proverbs 30:31)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:02.644309963Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}